chore(quality): make psalm + phpstan real in check:strict

`check:strict` ran its 8 steps in a for-loop that already propagated exit
codes, but `psalm` and `phpstan` each ended in `|| echo '... skipping ...'`
so both always exited 0 — two of the three static analysers were dead.
Removed the `|| echo` from both. `phpmd` was already real.

`test:all` is deliberately left dead: measuring its cost needs a running
Nextcloud environment, which this change does not have. Not flipped
unmeasured.

Findings the repaired gate surfaces (PHP 8.3.32, matching CI's pinned
php-version, in nextcloud:32-apache):

- check:no-legacy-types  PASS
- check:routes           2 orphans -> FALSE POSITIVE, script fixed
- lint                   0
- phpcs                  0 errors / 288 warnings (non-fatal by ruleset)
- phpmd                  0 (existing 306-entry baseline absorbs all)
- psalm                  6  -> config entries, no baseline
- phpstan                74 -> 2 general + 72 file; see below

phpstan's 2 *general* errors ("cannot be ignored, use excludePaths
instead") abort the run regardless of any baseline, so they had to be
fixed in config: OpenConnectorMetricsProvider and
AbstractCategoryAdapterProvider extend/implement OpenRegister types that
exist only at runtime. Added to excludePaths, same pattern the file
already uses for SynchronizationContractProvider.

41 of the file errors were one systemic false positive: every
`#[AuthorizedAdminSetting(OpenConnectorAdmin::class)]` resolves to a plain
`string` because lib/Settings/OpenConnectorAdmin.php is itself excluded, so
phpstan cannot see it implements IDelegatedSettings. Documented ignore
rather than 41 opaque baseline lines. Plus the cross-app @throws ignore
opencatalogi already carries.

That leaves 24, baselined with the debt they represent stated in the
tracking issue: 13 dead-code (unused constants / write-only properties /
unused method in RuleService + CloudEventListener), 7 redundant-or-
impossible `??` reads, and 4 misc. Two are worth fixing and are called out
in the issue: three `/*` block comments in BankfeedSyncService that were
meant to be `/**` docblocks (so their `@var` hints are inert, which is what
produces 6 of the `??` findings), and an `is_array()` guard in
SynchronizationService::processSyncRule() that can never fire because the
value is `(string)`-cast on the line above — the intended "config is an
array" error path is unreachable.

Regenerating the baseline also dropped 17 stale entries, several of which
only ever existed because symfony/expression-language and
symfony/dom-crawler were missing from the analysis vendor tree.

check:routes reported genericPreferences#get/setPreference as orphans. They
are not: Application.php registers that controller as a DI service under the
standard `OCA\OpenConnector\Controller\…` key (the class name NC synthesises
from the plain route name), so it resolves at runtime with no file under
lib/Controller/. The script was filesystem-only. Made it read
registerService() aliases out of Application.php — whitelisting exactly one
controller here, and still failing on a genuinely deleted controller
(verified by removing JobsController.php: 3 orphans, exit 1).
